rem Factorial Trailing Digits
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=160
rem Find the last five digits before the
rem trailing zeros of N!

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 1000000000000

rem Drop the factors 5 level by level:
rem N! = 5^e times the product P of the
rem n // 5^j parts with 5 removed. The
rem leftover power of 2 is divisible by
rem 32, so the digits are 0 mod 32 and
rem P / 2^e mod 3125; combine them.
Pre = array shape 3125 fill 1
for R in 1 to 3124
  Mul = (R mod 5 equal 0) choose 1 R
  Pre R = Pre (R - 1) * Mul mod 3125
end
Js = 0 to 17 array
Nj = N // 5 ** Js
Odd = (Nj // 3125) mod 2 equal 1
Sign = Odd choose 3124 1
F = Sign * (Pre (Nj mod 3125)) mod 3125
P = F reduce * mod 3125
E = Nj drop 1 sum
Half = 1563 E 3125 powmod
Low = P * Half mod 3125
Answer = 32 * (Low * 293 mod 3125)
Answer print
